  { id: 2, surahNumber: 1, ayahNumber: 2, arabic: "الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ", transliteration: "Alhamdu lillahi Rabbil 'alamin", english: "All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds.", tafheem: "This verse establishes the fundamental principle of Tawhid. Allah alone deserves all praise because He is the Creator, Sustainer, and Lord of all the worlds. 'Alamin' refers to everything that exists besides Allah — the heavens, the earth, and all creatures." },
  { id: 3, surahNumber: 1, ayahNumber: 3, arabic: "الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ", transliteration: "Ar-Rahmani r-Rahim", english: "The Entirely Merciful, the Especially Merciful.", tafheem: "These attributes emphasize Allah's boundless mercy. Ar-Rahman refers to mercy that encompasses everything in this world, while Ar-Rahim refers to the special mercy reserved for believers in the Hereafter. Tafheem teaches that Allah's mercy precedes His wrath." },
  { id: 4, surahNumber: 1, ayahNumber: 4, arabic: "مَالِكِ يَوْمِ الدِّينِ", transliteration: "Maliki yawmi d-din", english: "Sovereign of the Day of Recompense.", tafheem: "This verse reminds humanity of the inevitable Day of Judgment. Allah is the sole Master and Judge on that day. It is a powerful warning against heedlessness and a call to live with accountability." },
