  // Al-Falaq & An-Nas (Protection Surahs)
  { id: 15, surahNumber: 113, ayahNumber: 1, arabic: "قُلْ أَعُوذُ بِرَبِّ الْفَلَقِ", transliteration: "Qul a'udhu bi Rabbi l-falaq", english: "Say, 'I seek refuge in the Lord of daybreak'", tafheem: "Surah Al-Falaq and An-Nas are called Mu'awwidhatayn. They are recited for protection from all evils. Seeking refuge in Allah, the Creator of the dawn, protects from darkness and harm." },
  { id: 16, surahNumber: 113, ayahNumber: 2, arabic: "مِنْ شَرِّ مَا خَلَقَ", transliteration: "Min sharri ma khalaq", english: "From the evil of that which He created", tafheem: "We seek Allah's protection from all evils that exist in creation — whether physical or spiritual. Tafheem notes the importance of recognizing evil forces." },
  { id: 17, surahNumber: 113, ayahNumber: 3, arabic: "وَمِنْ شَرِّ غَاسِقٍ إِذَا وَقَبَ", transliteration: "Wa min sharri ghasiqin idha waqab", english: "And from the evil of darkness when it settles", tafheem: "Protection from the evil of nightfall and the hidden dangers it brings. Nighttime is often associated with harmful forces." },
