  { id: 31, surahNumber: 36, ayahNumber: 6, arabic: "لِتُنذِرَ قَوْمًا مَّا أُنذِرَ آبَاؤُهُمْ فَهُمْ غَافِلُونَ", transliteration: "Litundhira qawman ma undhira aba'uhum fahum ghafilun", english: "That you may warn a people whose forefathers were not warned, so they are unaware.", tafheem: "The Arabs had not received a prophet for centuries. The Qur'an awakens them from their heedlessness." },
  { id: 32, surahNumber: 36, ayahNumber: 7, arabic: "لَقَدْ حَقَّ الْقَوْلُ عَلَىٰ أَكْثَرِهِمْ فَهُمْ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ", transliteration: "Laqad haqqal qawlu 'ala aktharihim fahum la yu'minun", english: "Already the word has come into effect upon most of them, so they do not believe.", tafheem: "Due to their persistent rejection, many people are destined for punishment. Yet the message must be delivered." },
  { id: 33, surahNumber: 36, ayahNumber: 8, arabic: "إِنَّا جَعَلْنَا فِي أَعْنَاقِهِمْ أَغْلَالًا فَهِيَ إِلَى الْأَذْقَانِ فَهُم مُّقْمَحُونَ", transliteration: "Inna ja'alna fi a'naqihim aghlalan fa hiya ilal adhqani fahum muqmahun", english: "Indeed, We have put shackles on their necks, and they are to their chins, so they are with heads [kept] aloft.", tafheem: "This powerful metaphor describes how the arrogant are unable to bow their heads in humility to Allah. Their pride prevents them from accepting guidance." },

  // Al-Baqarah (selected)
  { id: 34, surahNumber: 2, ayahNumber: 1, arabic: "الم", transliteration: "Alif-Lam-Mim", english: "Alif, Lam, Meem.", tafheem: "These letters are from the mutashabihat. Their true meaning is known only to Allah. They serve as a challenge and reminder of the miraculous nature of the Qur'an." },
  { id: 35, surahNumber: 2, ayahNumber: 2, arabic: "ذَٰلِكَ الْكِتَابُ لَا رَيْبَ ۛ فِيهِ ۛ هُدًى لِّلْمُتَّقِينَ", transliteration: "Dhalikal kitabu la rayba fihi hudal lil-muttaqin", english: "This is the Book about which there is no doubt, a guidance for those conscious of Allah.", tafheem: "The Qur'an is free of doubt. It is guidance for the God-fearing. Tafheem explains that only those who fear Allah can truly benefit from its wisdom." },
  { id: 36, surahNumber: 2, ayahNumber: 3, arabic: "الَّذِينَ يُؤْمِنُونَ بِالْغَيْبِ وَيُقِيمُونَ الصَّلَاةَ وَمِمَّا رَزَقْنَاهُمْ يُنفِقُونَ", transliteration: "Alladhina yu'minuna bil-ghaybi wa yuqimunas-salata wa mimma razaqnahum yunfiqun", english: "Who believe in the unseen, establish prayer, and spend out of what We have provided for them,", tafheem: "The qualities of the righteous: belief in the unseen (including Allah, angels, afterlife), regular prayer, and charity. These form the foundation of a believer's life." },
  { id: 37, surahNumber: 2, ayahNumber: 4, arabic: "وَالَّذِينَ يُؤْمِنُونَ بِمَا أُنزِلَ إِلَيْكَ وَمَا أُنزِلَ مِن قَبْلِكَ وَبِالْآخِرَةِ هُمْ يُوقِنُونَ", transliteration: "Walladhina yu'minuna bima unzila ilayka wa ma unzila min qablika wa bil-akhirati hum yuqinun", english: "And who believe in what has been revealed to you, [O Muhammad], and what was revealed before you, and of the Hereafter they are certain.", tafheem: "True faith includes belief in all previous revelations and certainty about the Hereafter. Tafheem stresses the continuity of divine guidance." },
  { id: 38, surahNumber: 2, ayahNumber: 5, arabic: "أُولَٰئِكَ عَلَىٰ هُدًى مِّن رَّبِّهِمْ ۖ وَأُولَٰئِكَ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُونَ", transliteration: "Ula'ika 'ala hudan min Rabbihim wa ula'ika humul muflihun", english: "Those are upon [right] guidance from their Lord, and it is those who are the successful.", tafheem: "Those who possess these qualities receive guidance from Allah and attain true success in both worlds. The Tafheem declares them the truly successful people." },

  // Al-Mulk
  { id: 39, surahNumber: 67, ayahNumber: 1, arabic: "تَبَارَكَ الَّذِي بِيَدِهِ الْمُلْكُ وَهُوَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ", transliteration: "Tabarakalladhi biyadihil mulku wa huwa 'ala kulli shay'in qadir", english: "Blessed is He in whose hand is dominion, and He is over all things competent.", tafheem: "This surah begins by declaring Allah's absolute sovereignty over the entire universe. Tafheem explains that true power and kingship belongs only to Allah." },
  { id: 40, surahNumber: 67, ayahNumber: 2, arabic: "الَّذِي خَلَقَ الْمَوْتَ وَالْحَيَاةَ لِيَبْلُوَكُمْ أَيُّكُمْ أَحْسَنُ عَمَلًا", transliteration: "Alladhi khalaqal mawta wal hayata liyabluwakum ayyukum ahsanu 'amala", english: "[He] who created death and life to test you [as to] which of you is best in deed.", tafheem: "The purpose of life and death is to test which of us performs the best deeds. This is one of the most profound verses explaining the philosophy of life." },
  { id: 41, surahNumber: 67, ayahNumber: 3, arabic: "الَّذِي خَلَقَ سَبْعَ سَمَاوَاتٍ طِبَاقًا ۖ مَّا تَرَىٰ فِي خَلْقِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ مِن تَفَاوُتٍ", transliteration: "Alladhi khalaqa sab'a samawatin tibaqan ma tara fi khalqir Rahman min tafawut", english: "[And] who created seven heavens in layers. You do not see in the creation of the Most Merciful any inconsistency.", tafheem: "The perfect harmony and order of the universe is evidence of a single, wise Creator. Tafheem highlights the flawless design of the cosmos." },
  { id: 42, surahNumber: 67, ayahNumber: 4, arabic: "ثُمَّ ارْجِعِ الْبَصَرَ كَرَّتَيْنِ يَنقَلِبْ إِلَيْكَ الْبَصَرُ خَاسِئًا وَهُوَ حَسِيرٌ", transliteration: "Thummarji'il basara karratayni yanqalib ilaykal basaru khasi'an wa huwa hasir", english: "Then return [your] vision twice again. [Your] vision will return to you humbled while it is fatigued.", tafheem: "Even if you examine the heavens repeatedly, you will never find any flaw. This is a powerful challenge to those who deny the Creator." },
  { id: 43, surahNumber: 67, ayahNumber: 5, arabic: "وَلَقَدْ زَيَّنَّا السَّمَاءَ الدُّنْيَا بِمَصَابِيحَ", transliteration: "Wa laqad zayyannas sama'ad dunya bimasabih", english: "And We have certainly beautified the nearest heaven with stars.", tafheem: "The stars are described both as decoration and as missiles against devils. Tafheem explains the dual purpose of the celestial bodies." },

